 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 457849,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Two cards are selected at random from a standard 52-card deck. Find the probability that the second card is an Ace, given that the first card selected was an Ace (assume the first card is not replaced before selecting the second card). Round your answer to 4 decimal places.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\mathrm{Probability}=0.005\"></span> "
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "Since we are interested in the probability that the first card is an ace and the second card is also an ace, we can use the following probability formula:<br>\n<span data-math=\"P\\left( {A\\;\\mathrm{and}\\;B} \\right) = P\\left( A \\right)\\cdot P\\left( {B\\;|\\;A} \\right),\\;\\mathrm{when}\\;A,\\;B\\;\\mathrm{are}\\;\\mathrm{dependent}\\;\\mathrm{events}\"></span><br>\nIn this example, <span data-math=\"P(A)\"></span> is the probability of selecting an Ace on the first card selection, which is <span data-math=\"\\frac{4}{{52}}\"></span>, since there are four Aces in the standard 52-card deck. The probability of getting an Ace on the second card, given that an Ace was selected on the first card, can be calculated as <span data-math=\"\\frac{3}{{51}}\"></span> since there are three Aces remaining in the deck and there are 51 cards remaining in the deck since the first card was not replaced before selecting the second card.<br><br>\nCalculate the probability that the second card is an Ace, given that the first card selected was an Ace, as follows:<br>\n<span data-math=\"P\\left( {A\\;\\mathrm{and}\\;B} \\right) = P\\left( A \\right)\\cdot P\\left( {B\\;|\\;A} \\right)\"></span><br>\n<span data-math=\"P\\left( {A\\;\\mathrm{and}\\;B} \\right) = \\frac{4}{{52}}\\cdot\\frac{3}{{51}} = \\frac{{12}}{{2,652}} = 0.0045\">\n\n\n</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
